# NISAR SAR Earth Observation Platform — Environment Configuration
# Copy to .env and configure your keys.
#
# Easiest path: Run the app and paste keys into the in-app Provider Settings
# panel (the POWER UP chip, bottom-right) — it writes this checkout's .env for you
# and restarts the dev server.
#
# NOTE ON CLIENT-EXPOSED KEYS: GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY and CESIUM_ION_TOKEN are
# injected into the browser bundle by design (they are used client-side) and
# will be visible in browser devtools. Restrict/scope them in your provider consoles.
# All other keys below remain strictly server-side.

# Optional: Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles and place search.
# CLIENT-EXPOSED — restrict it (HTTP referrer + API restriction) in Google Cloud.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional: Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles through Cesium ion, Bing world
# imagery, and Cesium World Terrain.
# CLIENT-EXPOSED — use a public assets:read token with URL restrictions.
CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=

# Optional: NASA FIRMS live active fire detections.
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY (never exposed to browser — polled via /api/firms proxy).
# Obtain a free key at: https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/
# Without a key, the Active Fires layer indicates "KEY REQUIRED".
FIRMS_MAP_KEY=

# Optional: OpenAI API key for concise HUD location telemetry summaries.
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. If omitted, the HUD operates keylessly without summary text.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_HUD_SUMMARY_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Dev server network binding.
# Default is localhost (safe default — reachable only from this machine).
# Set HOST=0.0.0.0 to bind on your local network.
PORT=4173
HOST=localhost
